public/monaco/
# Pyodide's self-hosted runtime (npm run sync:pyodide-runtime, wired into
# predev/prebuild exactly like the two above) — a straight copy of 7 files,
# 12 MB, out of node_modules/pyodide, which package-lock.json already pins.
#
# It used to be committed, which made it the odd one out among these three and
# cost real CI time: `pyodideRuntimeSync.driftguard.test.ts` asserted the
# committed copy was byte-identical to the installed package, so EVERY
# dependabot pyodide bump failed 6 of 7 assertions by construction — dependabot
# can bump the package but cannot run a `cp` or commit 12 MB of binaries
# (2026-09-22, PR #709). Not committing it is what makes that drift impossible;
# see pyodideRuntimeSync.notcommitted.test.ts, which keeps it that way.
#
# NOTE: public/pyodide-shims/ stays tracked — those are copies of OUR OWN
# source (src/services/python/pyodide/shims/**/*.py), not a vendored package.
public/pyodide/

