# Downloaded library documents (PDFs/HTML) — extraction input only, NOT published
# (third-party copyright). The app links to the external source URL instead.
# RELOCATED 2026-07-12: raw documents now live in
# pqctoday-priv/local-evidence-cache/library/ (see
# maintenance/LOCAL-FILES-REMEDIATION-PLAN-07122026.md in the private repo) —
# this repo's public/library/ should never hold raw content again; the ignore
# rule stays as a defensive backstop for any script not yet updated.
# .md summaries + manifest.json are tracked (manifest.json newly re-included
# 2026-07-12 — was silently excluded before, breaking the doc-grounding trust
# score dimension for this source; every other source's manifest was already
# tracked, this was the one gap).
public/library/*
!public/library/*.md
!public/library/manifest.json

# Downloaded product documents (generated by scripts/download-products.js).
# RELOCATED 2026-07-12, same reasoning as library above.
# Switched from a bare directory-level ignore to a per-content ignore
# (matching library's pattern) so manifest.json can be re-included — a bare
# ignore can't selectively re-include files within it, which is why this used
# to have no !re-inclusion rules at all. The old bare rule's reason (protecting
# against a worktree-convenience SYMLINK, main already dropped one such
# committed symlink in 2c341c9f) no longer applies: no worktree needs its own
# populated public/products/ anymore now that raw content lives in priv, so
# there's nothing left for a convenience symlink to protect.
public/products/*
!public/products/*.md
!public/products/manifest.json
!public/products/manifest-full-591.json
!public/products/skip-list.json

# Downloaded Common Criteria evaluation documents (generated by scrape-compliance.ts)
# Currently empty in every known checkout — left as a bare ignore (unpopulated,
# nothing to reconcile) but flagged here: if this ever gets populated, it needs
# the same RELOCATED treatment as library/products above, not a silent re-scatter.
public/cc/

# Catalog proof files (HTML/PDF — downloaded locally; manifest.json + skip-list.json are tracked)
