# Local-gate receipts: `.gate-ok-<short sha>` is written by `npm run
# gate:release` / .husky/pre-push only when every step passed on that commit,
# and read by the pre-push hook to skip a gate it already ran. Per-machine;
# never committed. See GATES.md.
.gate-ok-*

# Release freeze manifest tool (release:freeze) and its test.
!scripts/release-freeze.ts
!scripts/release-freeze.test.ts
# NIST SP 800-90B estimator tool -> WebAssembly (entropy workshop W0/W1/D4,
# 2026-09-24). Reproducible build (Dockerfile.wasm + build/stage scripts), the
# glibc ldbl-128 shim, the D4 synthetic-dataset generator and the W1 parity
# harness. They build/verify the committed public/wasm/entropy90b/ artefacts,
# so every checkout needs them. Checked with `git check-ignore -v` per the
# habit recorded above.
!scripts/entropy-90b/
# A bare `build-wasm.sh` pattern above ignores every file of that name.
!scripts/entropy-90b/build-wasm.sh
# The scripts that MAKE src/data/validation/vector-manifest.json's verification
# claims runnable (scripts/acvp/README.md explains the mapping): the byte-copying
# subset reproducer the manifest's source.verification.method cites, and the four
# independent Python cross-checks the HKDF / KBKDF / SHA-MCT / AES-CBC-MCT vector
# files cite in _provenance.construction_note. They are referenced by committed
# package.json scripts (acvp:subset-reproduce, acvp:crosschecks), so they have the
# same `scripts/*` trap as every entry above: without this negation `git add
# scripts/acvp/...` is a SILENT no-op and the provenance record goes back to being
# an unreproducible self-assertion. Verified with `git check-ignore -v` on each file.
!scripts/acvp/
# ...but not the interpreter's byte-cache, which the negation above would let in.
scripts/acvp/__pycache__/
